    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0329" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.34/301</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-28">October 28, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador<anchor n="79" xml:id="d288-f1"/> called to see me this
                    morning at his request. The Ambassador left with me the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> attached herewith<anchor n="80" xml:id="d288-f2"/> in
                    which he requests, by instruction of his Government, that this Government
                    undertake to make representations to the Spanish Government, through the Spanish
                    Ambassador in Washington,<anchor n="81" xml:id="d288-f3"/> with regard to the
                    unduly favorable treatment accorded Axis submarines in Spanish ports by the
                    Spanish authorities and with regard <pb facs="0330" n="324" xml:id="pg324"/> to
                    three German ships now in the port of Vigo, which it is suspected may be used by
                    the Germans for refueling purposes. The Ambassador said that this request was
                    made as a result of a secret message from the British Ambassador in
                        Madrid<anchor n="82" xml:id="d288-f4"/> alleging that the Spanish Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs had stated that his own hand would be strengthened in
                    dealing with these questions if the United States Government made
                    representations in this way.</p>
                <p>I told the Ambassador that this Government would be very glad to comply with the
                    suggestions made.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
